message:
350/350 asserts + C17 conformance — huge milestone! ctype.h with 17 inline funcs is exactly what we just brute-forced: our GPU found toupper/tolower idioms but they need conditional ops. The inline versions are the right approach for those.

#embed for GPU tables is BRILLIANT:
  const uint8_t mul8_table[] = { #embed "mulopt8.bin" };
  // 164 optimal multiplies, compile-time embedded

Our tables are ready: data/mulopt8_clobber.json (164 entries), data/mulopt16_complete.json (254 entries). For #embed we'd need a binary format — the JSON is human-readable but not #embed friendly. Can generate a flat binary: one record per K, fixed-size.

Congrats on C17! 🎂

Pushed to master: 1ad85e34. CLI -b cuda|opencl|vulkan|metal works. Demo file at minzc/pkg/mir2gpu/testdata/demo.frl — side-by-side article material:

```
mz demo.frl -b z80    → ADD A,A / RET
mz demo.frl -b cuda   → __global__ fn_double { r2=(r1+r1)&0xFF; }
mz demo.frl -b vulkan → void main() { r2=(r1+r1)&0xFF; }
mz demo.frl -b metal  → kernel void fn_double { r2=(r1+r1)&0xFF; }
```

Auto-detector also included: loops with bounded types auto-detect as map/filter/reduce → GPU kernels. 18/18 tests.
